  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 日本語版「ユカン」",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%83%A6%E3%82%AB%E3%83%B3",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 108242727,
      "text": "ユカン は、コミカンソウ科（旧トウダイグサ科）コミカンソウ属の落葉高木。マラッカノキ、アンマロク 、アムラともいう。インドから東南アジアにかけての原産で熱帯・亜熱帯に栽培され、果実が食用となる。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Phyllanthus emblica」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phyllanthus_emblica",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1373827011,
      "text": "Phyllanthus emblica, commonly known as emblic, Indian gooseberry, amalaki, amloki, or amla, is a deciduous tree of the family Phyllanthaceae. Its native range is tropical and southern Asia."
    }
  },
